  <Requirements>
    <Sets DefaultMinVersion="1.1">
      <!--
        1.4 DRAWS A CHART; 1.8 IS WHERE ONE ARRIVES AS A CHART. Raised from 1.4
        on 2026-09-13, deliberately, and this is the reasoning so nobody lowers
        it back on reach grounds alone.

        1.4 is what the shapes need (ShapeCollection.addGeometricShape / addLine
        / addTextBox) and it is not enough. `Shape.group` needs 1.8, so below it
        a chart lands as ~40 LOOSE SHAPES — and nothing tells the user: there is
        no mention of 1.8 anywhere in the message catalogue, while the re-edit
        path says "select an inserted chart group first", naming a group that
        host cannot make. `canInsertPicture` is 1.8 too, so the picture fallback
        for undrawable marks does not exist below it either.

        WHAT IT COSTS, measured against Microsoft's update history on
        2026-09-08: nothing on any serviced Microsoft 365 channel. Current
        (2608, 20326.20144), Monthly Enterprise (2608/2607/2606) and
        Semi-Annual Enterprise (2608/2607/2606) are ALL far above the 18730
        that 1.8 needs — and above the 19610 that 1.10 needs. What this excludes
        is volume-licensed/LTSC, which Microsoft lists "Not available" for 1.6
        onward and which therefore can never reach 1.8 by updating, plus
        out-of-support installs and Mac below 16.96.

        AND NOT 1.10, though on Windows it would cost the same. 1.10 buys
        rotation, so pie/doughnut/sunburst and CAGR arrows draw natively rather
        than arriving as a complete picture with a message. That is a real
        difference for exactly three of 25 chart kinds, and at 1.8 the outcome
        is honest and whole. The extra exclusion 1.10 would add is Mac
        16.96-16.104, which is a live, updating population. 1.8 is the lowest
        floor at which this add-in is coherent; going higher buys polish at
        someone's expense.
      -->
      <Set Name="PowerPointApi" MinVersion="1.8" />
    </Sets>
  </Requirements>

